# Excel testcase and input workbooks

Read `Commons/excel_testcase/README.md`, the target app's registered profile, and
a current nearby testcase/input pair. Preserve the parser's actual contract.

## Testcase workbook

- New cases use the registered app's Excel workflow. Do not create a parallel
  Python test merely to bypass Excel collection or action dispatch.
- Use the `Steps` sheet with columns `Input Excel`, `Action`, `Page`, `Params`,
  `Filter`. Row 2 identifies the input workbook; executable steps start at row 3.
- Use supported profile/shared actions. Filter group/value tokens must resolve
  through the target app's object repository. Use actual callable method names.
- Put cases in that profile's `case_subdirs`; preserve existing app-specific
  folder layouts. Add the case to the intended suite where needed.
- End comparison cases with the framework's failure assertion so earlier
  mismatches cannot be silently discarded.
- Static checks use the existing static workbook/profile contract; do not force
  them into TabQuery format or require a query workbook for every functional case.

## Query input workbook

- Store queries in `InputFiles/<APP>/`. Follow the neighboring workbook's first
  sheet headers: `TabName`, `TabQuery`, `StatQuery`, and its supported output-name
  columns. `Commons/query_reader.py` is the authority on accepted aliases.
- Match `TabName` to the adapter's `TabSpec.input_tab`. Match selected column
  aliases/order to the columns retained by the app's table reader.
- Supply the stat query for numeric comparisons, with aliases matching the app's
  stat names. Respect `Config/tab_setting.yaml`: deterministic sort before the
  tab row limit, and no pagination/row limit on total stat counts.
- Follow `expected-data.mdc` for every SQL/Cypher query; do not embed UI-captured
  expected counts, selected row IDs, or unrelated copied filters.

## Naming and formatting

- Preserve established naming per application; do not enforce PSDC naming across
  other projects. For a new paired case, use the same testcase/input basename
  unless that app has a documented exception. Follow the latest user-specified
  filename and capitalization exactly.
- On a rename, update the actual input filename, `Steps!A2`, stored UI/DB output
  filenames, and direct documentation/suite references. Keep study/filter IDs in
  SQL and steps unchanged unless the requested cohort itself changes.
- Handle case-only filesystem renames safely; never delete the destination via
  an old path that refers to the same file on a case-insensitive filesystem.
- Keep cell gridlines visible in created/updated testcase and input sheets.
  Preserve unrelated styles, column widths, sheets, dropdowns, and freeze panes.
- Retain identifiers as text, including leading zeros. Store SQL/Cypher as text
  with readable formatting. Do not add presentation sheets or merge parser cells.

## Verification

- Reopen saved workbooks; verify contents, names, gridlines, and validations.
  Resolve input paths, tab query names, actions, and repository keys.
- Check pytest collection/suite membership when adding a case. Run the actual
  case when its environment and expected data are available.
- For failures, inspect the matching UI/expected output sheets and exact records.
  Separate data drift, scraper defects, query defects, and UI readiness issues.
